## FORMULAS & CALCULATIONS

[calc-00002] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: For sample size calculations, always incorporate the Finite Population Correction (FPC) factor: n_adj = n / (1 + (n - 1) / N), where n is the initial sample size and N is the population size.
## CODE SNIPPETS & TEMPLATES

[code-00001] helpful=0 harmful=0 :: When generating Excel files via Python, always wrap the file-writing process in a structure that ensures the file is saved and closed. Explicitly call `writer.close()` or `wb.save()` at the very end of the script, and verify the logic flow does not terminate prematurely.
